  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1: Possible record highs Wednesday.\n\nLook for 5h heights to build head into midweek with westerly\nflow aiding in heating up the lower levels. Highs Wednesday are\nlikely to reach close to or even exceed records. See climate\nsection below.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Front arrives Thursday with mainly a mountain \nthreat of showers/few storms, followed by a stronger front \nFriday with much cooler weather for the weekend.\n\nUpper ridge starts to flatten ahead of a front Thursday. Models\nare in agreement that the mountains will be having a better\nprobability for having measurable showers/few storms compared to\nthe Piedmont. Some modest instability may occur, but overall\nmore organized and stronger convection looks to stay north of\nthe forecast area. Some short range guidance also showing a\nbackdoor front sinking into the northern portions of the\nforecast area on Thursday, which could keep temperatures a bit\ncooler than previously forecast.\n\nA much stronger front arrives on Friday, with a sharp cool down\nfor the weekend following the frontal passage. Not much rain \nwill be associated with the Friday frontal passage...with the \ngreatest chance remaining over the western mountains. Much more \nisolated chance east of the mountains. This could be the first \nfreeze of the season for the mountains with frost in the \nPiedmont on Sunday morning as high pressure builds directly \noverhead.",
